dsv41 patch 0057 (20.10.2026): paired KV pages. The ratio-1 compressed-KV group stops paying the ratio-2 group's block
stride. Base: the v6 files (vllm/models/deepseek_v41/attention.py incl. our 0051, vllm/v1/worker/utils.py incl. 0053).
Why: vLLM packs every KV cache group of a model into one shared block pool (packed BLHNC layout), and the block stride is
the widest group's page sum. On DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash that is the ratio-2 group: 3 compressed-KV pages (layers 2/8/14) + 3
indexer pages per 128 tokens = 138,240 B. Indexer key caches exist only on the four KV-source layers 2/8/14/20 (24/28/32/36
read layer 20's). The ratio-1 group (layer 20's compressed KV + indexer page) holds 46,080 B per 64 tokens but paid the
full stride for every block, so two thirds of each of its blocks stayed empty. Per token and node, as charged for a
max-length request: 1,462.5 B fp8_ds_mla records (584 B a state) + 337.5 B FP8 indexer keys (132 B a state) = 1,800 B
data, 1,440 B padding, 829 B sliding-window admission reserve (15 SWA groups x 131 blocks a request) = 4,069 B.
How: the ratio-1 specs take 128-token manager blocks (block_size 128) made of two 64-state kernel pages
(storage_block_size 64; the SM12x kernels keep their 64 states per page). create_kv_cache_views views each manager block
of that group as two kernel blocks of half the stride, with the same per-page layout as an unpaired block (layer offsets
and strides halved); the GPU runner already expands manager blocks into kernel blocks in the block table and slot mapping
(BlockTables.blocks_per_kv_block), and every kernel in the path addresses pages through the view's stride(0) (FlashInfer
SM120 sparse MLA, our Triton verify kernel, DeepGEMM paged MQA logits, rope_quant_insert). Paired and unpaired pages never
share a group (MLAAttentionSpec.is_uniform_with_collection). A paired block (2 x 46,080 = 92,160 B) fits under the
ratio-2 stride, which stays 138,240 B, so the ratio-1 group is charged 1,080 instead of 2,160 B per token. A paired page
must be exactly two kernel pages including their alignment padding; _dsv41_check_pair sets page_size_padded where the
128-state page aligns differently (the indexer page under patch 0059's 512 B alignment: 16,896 vs 2 x 8,704 B).
VLLM_DSV41_KV_SWA_FILL fills the sliding-window groups up to the stride (more layers per group, fewer groups, a smaller
admission reserve a request). With FP8 KV a fourth SWA layer (4 x 37,440 B) does not fit under 138,240 B, so it changes
nothing; with patch 0059 (NVFP4 records) it does.
Measured (20.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v8, 3.75 GiB KV pool per node, one window; no switches against both):
KV pool 989,460 -> 1,346,928 tokens (+36.1 %; 29,127 blocks either way); bytes per token live (250K-token prompt,
kv_cache_usage_perc x pool / prompt tokens) 3,267 -> 2,187 (-33 %); cost per verify round, geometric mean of 14 cells,
-0.31 % (worst cell +1.2 %), tok/s +0.33 %; T=0 texts identical 8/8; corruption test (8K/30K/50K/100K, 4 each) 0 hits;
suite prose / code 54.3 / 97.7 -> 54.1 / 98.4 tok/s.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_KV_PAIR=1 (default 0 = off), VLLM_DSV41_KV_SWA_FILL=1 (default 0). Raises with indexer_sparse_logits
or the ROCm MXFP4 indexer (not covered; the alignment code only aligns the full stride).

